{"tool_name":"aromtool","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"aromtool","home":"https://github.com/hewg2008/AromTool","summary":"Predicting aromatic stacking energy using an atomic neural network model.","addition_date":"2021-11-18T19:21:48.508835Z","last_update_date":"2021-11-18T19:21:48.511342Z","tool_type":["Library"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:aromtool","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"name":"Ruibo Wu","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1984-046X"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"public"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Network analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3927"},{"term":"Small molecule design","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_4009"}]}],"name":"AromTool","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"Chan019","publication":[{"doi":"10.1039/D1CP01954F","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 the Owner Societies.Aromatic stacking exists widely and plays important roles in protein-ligand interactions. Computational tools to automatically analyze the geometry and accurately calculate the energy of stacking interactions are desired for structure-based drug design. Herein, we employed a Behler-Parrinello neural network (BPNN) to build predictive models for aromatic stacking interactions and further integrated it into an open-source Python package named AromTool for benzene-containing aromatic stacking analysis. Based on extensive testing, AromTool presents desirable precision in comparison to DFT calculations and excellent efficiency for high-throughput aromatic stacking analysis of protein-ligand complexes. This journal is","authors":[{"name":"Diao H."},{"name":"He W."},{"name":"Liang D."},{"name":"Lyu N."},{"name":"Wang K."},{"name":"Wu R."}],"date":"2021-08-14T00:00:00Z","journal":"Physical Chemistry Chemical Physics","title":"AromTool: Predicting aromatic stacking energy using an atomic neural network model"},"pmid":"34286738"}],"topic":[{"term":"Machine lear